    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27wdcZpy5tWFoUfsGvALeMr)_\n\nBefore: all 180 literate docs sat flat in `docs/tangles/`, while the modules they produce are grouped in `libraries/modules/` subdirectories.\n\nAfter: each module doc is in the matching subdirectory of `docs/tangles/` (`academic/`, `base/`, `base/navi/`, `custom/`, `env/`, `funct/`, `media/`, `prog/`, `text/`, `tooling/`, `ui/`), next to its `-old.org` predecessor. The older topic notes that have no module (`org-config.org`, `search.org` and so on, plus `sp-typesetting.org`, `sp-typst.org`, `sp-helper-functions.org`, `sp-appearance-overview.org` and `sp-music-composition.org`) stay at the top of `docs/tangles/`.\n\nHow: the 145 docs are moved with `git mv`. Their tangle paths and README links gain the extra `../`, relative links to the older notes are adjusted, the module tree in `docs/main.org` links to the new locations, and the tangle-all block and shell one-liner in `README.org` now search `docs/tangles/` recursively (and avoid backslashes, so the one-liner also works in fish). I ran the new tangle-all command on a copy: it tangles 131 docs and produces the same `.el` files as the old layout on `main`, apart from `sp-org-issues.el` being in `custom/`.\n\nThis PR is based on #9, because `sp-org-issues` is moved there. Retarget it to `main` once #9 is merged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_013V6WSXthgpc9jPWyZsevsf)_",
